Found during fresh-install testing: the installed desktop app couldn't do Android because build.ps1 built the sidecar CLI (target/release/xpressclaw.exe, copied to tauri/binaries) WITHOUT --features android. The Tauri crate itself needs no android feature - it spawns the CLI as a sidecar (main.rs 'spawn sidecar'); Android comes entirely from that CLI. So the one-line gap was the sidecar build flag. This is the 'plumb android across ... tauri' piece ADR-024's Risks section flagged. Flag is opt-in (default build stays android-free). Verified: built installer's sidecar responds to 'android --help', and /v1/android/status works in the installed app.
